{"duration_api_ms":123353,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"83e0aa8d-708c-4fbd-87a6-d2241c155d03","total_cost_usd":0.089532,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11841,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":13168,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10678},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":13168,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":13168,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11841,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.089532,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":10678,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence—a group of easy to remember words—for the generation of deterministic UTXOs. It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\n\\nThis BIP falls under the GPL License.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to handling raw binary or hexadecimal representations of wallet keys. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone. This guide provides a way to transport computer-generated wallet data with a human-readable transcription. It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the Mnemonic\\n\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in multiples of 32 bits. With more entropy, security is improved, but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\n  \"decisions\": [],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence—a group of easy to remember words—for the generation of deterministic UTXOs.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Combined with a4-a5 and corrected UTOX to UTXO\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into abstract with ASCII corrected to binary\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into abstract\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to handling raw binary or hexadecimal representations of wallet keys.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into motivation; satoshis corrected to keys\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a10\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into motivation section\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a11\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This guide provides a way to transport computer-generated wallet data with a human-readable transcription.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into motivation with improved clarity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into motivation; süeed corrected to seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Generating the Mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"Memonic corrected to Mnemonic; made section heading\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in multiples of 32 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Demonic→mnemonic; multiple of 23→multiples of 32\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"With more entropy, security is improved, but the sentence length increases.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into generating section\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into flowing text\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"1024-2048 byts corrected to 128-256 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b6\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"First, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into procedure description\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"reason\": \"SHA652 corrected to SHA256\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b8\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This checksum is appended to the initial entropy.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into procedure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Groups of 12 bits corrected to 11 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b10\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated into procedure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b11\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Integrated as table introduction\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\",\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"for the generation of deterministic UTXOs\",\n      \"corrects\": \"for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"UTXO is standard Bitcoin term; UTOX not recognized\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"converting it into a binary seed\",\n      \"corrects\": \"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP 39 produces binary data, not ASCII text\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in multiples of 32 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The demonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 23 bits.\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP 39 uses 32-bit multiples; demonic is typo\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP 39 specifies 128-256 bits; byts should be bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"its SHA652 hash\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP 39 uses SHA256 algorithm, not SHA652\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"groups of 12 bits\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"11 bits encode 2048 values (0-2047); 12 would encode 4096\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to handling raw binary or hexadecimal representations of wallet keys.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"wallet satoshis\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP 39 derives keys and addresses, not satoshi amounts\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":105114,"type":"result","duration_ms":123416,"uuid":"a44942c2-ce87-4bff-8674-0309a3d74e59","ttft_stream_ms":1008,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":1009,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
